<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liutprand, King of the Lombards</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/744">744</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liutprand was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> from 712 to 744 and the most powerful of their kings. He strengthened royal authority over the dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spoleto">Spoleto</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benevento">Benevento</a>, added many laws to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-rothari">Edict of Rothari</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. His gift of the town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutri">Sutri</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ii">Pope Gregory II</a> in 728 is regarded as the first step towards the Papal States.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liutprand-king-of-the-lombards.jpg" alt="Liutprand, King of the Lombards" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luitprand_tremissis_661673.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 728 the Lombard king <b>Liutprand</b> handed the town of Sutri to Pope Gregory II, an act often seen as the first territorial grant to the papacy.</blockquote><a href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>King <b>Liutprand</b>'s gift of Sutri to the pope in 728 was its first territorial grant.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-rome">Duchy of Rome</a></li><li><blockquote>The dukes of Spoleto acted like rulers in their own right, waging war on the Byzantines and sometimes defying the Lombard kings; Transamund II was deposed by <b>Liutprand</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/duchy-of-spoleto">Duchy of Spoleto</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Liutprand</b> strengthened royal power and in 728 gave Sutri to the Pope, a step towards the Papal States.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Kingdom of the Lombards</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in Pavia, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.47,9.19&amp;year=734" aria-label="Milan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4768 560 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Liutprand, King of the Lombards"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.47,9.19&amp;year=734">What was here in 734 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
